#{[17592186115738 :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is obtained from $I_2$ by exactly one elementary row operation.\n\nMatrix $B$ is obtained by $R_2\\leftarrow4R_2$. Matrix $C$ is obtained by $R_2\\leftarrow R_2+2R_1$. Matrix $A$ requires both adding a multiple of row 1 to row 2 and scaling row 2, so it is not elementary.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ and $C$ only.\""] [17592186115763 :question/worked-solution "To find $A^2$, multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\nA^2=\\begin{bmatrix}3&2\\\\-4&7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3&2\\\\-4&7\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}9-8&6+14\\\\-12-28&-8+49\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}1&20\\\\-40&41\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186115815 :question/worked-solution "Interpret the constant term as a multiple of the identity matrix: $f(A)=A^2+2A-3I_2$. First,\n\n$$\nA^2=\\begin{bmatrix}1&-3\\\\4&0\\end{bmatrix}^2=\\begin{bmatrix}-11&-3\\\\4&-12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nf(A)=\\begin{bmatrix}-11&-3\\\\4&-12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2&-6\\\\8&0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3&0\\\\0&3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12&-9\\\\12&-15\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186115829 :question/worked-solution "Apply the distributive law $BA+BC=B(A+C)$. Here $C=-A$, so $A+C=0_{3\\times3}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B0_{3\\times3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0&0&0\\\\0&0&0\\\\0&0&0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186115835 :question/worked-solution "By the associative law, $ABC=A(BC)$. Compute the smaller product first:\n\n$$\nBC=\\begin{bmatrix}2&-1&-2\\\\5&-5&-5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\0\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $ABC=A\\begin{bmatrix}0\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0\\\\0\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186115840 :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ interchanges the two rows. To transform $E$ back into $I_2$, interchange the rows again. Applying that operation to the right half of $[E\\mid I_2]$ gives\n\n$$\nE^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186115854 :question/worked-solution "Write $A$ beside $I_3$ and perform the same row operations on both sides:\n\n$$\n[A\\mid I_3]=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1&-3&3&1&0&0\\\\0&1&2&0&1&0\\\\0&0&-1&0&0&1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nApply $R_3\\leftarrow-R_3$, then $R_2\\leftarrow R_2-2R_3$, then $R_1\\leftarrow R_1-3R_3$, and finally $R_1\\leftarrow R_1+3R_2$. This gives\n\n$$\n[I_3\\mid A^{-1}]=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|ccc}1&0&0&1&3&9\\\\0&1&0&0&1&2\\\\0&0&1&0&0&-1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1&3&9\\\\0&1&2\\\\0&0&-1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186115959 :question/worked-solution "To change the first entry of row 3 from $-4$ to $0$, add four times row 1:\n\n$$\nR_3\\leftarrow R_3+4R_1.\n$$\n\nTo change the second-row pivot from $5$ to $1$, multiply row 2 by $\\frac15$:\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftarrow\\frac15R_2.\n$$\n\nThese operations give exactly the two displayed intermediate matrices. The final operation $R_3\\leftarrow R_3+3R_2$ then produces $[I_3\\mid Q^{-1}]$."] [17592186120313 :question/worked-solution "To decide whether $b\\in\\operatorname{Col}(B)$, solve $B\\mathbf{x}=b$:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x_1-x_2&=1\\\\4x_1&=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe second equation gives $x_1=-1$. Substitution into the first gives $x_2=-3$. Thus the system is consistent, so $b\\in\\operatorname{Col}(B)$, and $x_1x_2=(-1)(-3)=3$."] [17592186120314 :question/worked-solution "Solve $C\\mathbf{x}=b$ using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&-1&3&2\\\\2&0&4&-1\\\\1&-3&0&7\\end{array}\\right]\n\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&-1&3&2\\\\0&2&-2&-5\\\\0&-2&-3&5\\end{array}\\right]\n\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1&-1&3&2\\\\0&2&-2&-5\\\\0&0&-5&0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nBack-substitution gives $x_3=0$, $x_2=-\\frac52$, and $x_1=-\\frac12$. The system is consistent, so $b\\in\\operatorname{Col}(C)$. Finally, $x_1x_2x_3=0$."] [17592186120357 :question/worked-solution "Find $x_1,x_2,x_3$ such that $x_1b_1+x_2b_2+x_3b_3=x$. The corresponding system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1+2x_2&=5\\\\-2x_1+x_2&=10\\\\4x_1-2x_2+3x_3&=-17.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding twice the first equation to the second gives $5x_2=20$, so $x_2=4$. Then $x_1=5-8=-3$. The third equation becomes $-12-8+3x_3=-17$, giving $x_3=1$.\n\nThus $[x]_B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\4\\\\1\\end{bmatrix}$, and $x_1+x_2+x_3=-3+4+1=2$."] [17592186120380 :question/worked-solution "Find $x_1,x_2$ such that $x_1b_1+x_2b_2=x$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_1-3x_2&=10\\\\4x_1-10x_2&=8\\\\-2x_1+6x_2&=-20.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubtracting four times the first equation from the second gives $2x_2=-32$, so $x_2=-16$. Then $x_1=10+3(-16)=-38$. These values also satisfy the third equation.\n\nTherefore, $[x]_B=\\begin{bmatrix}-38\\\\-16\\end{bmatrix}$ and $x_1+x_2=-54$."] [17592186120382 :question/worked-solution "The entries of $[x]_B$ are the coefficients of $b_1$ and $b_2$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nx=5b_1-7b_2=5\\begin{bmatrix}3\\\\2\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}2\\\\4\\\\3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}15-14\\\\10-28\\\\25-21\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\-18\\\\4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186120398 :question/worked-solution "For $b$ to lie in $\\operatorname{Col}(A)$, the system $A\\mathbf{x}=b$ must be consistent. Subtract twice row 1 from row 2 and five times row 1 from row 3:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1&-2&1\\\\2&-2&3\\\\5&-8&k\\end{array}\\right]\n\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1&-2&1\\\\0&2&1\\\\0&2&k-5\\end{array}\\right]\n\\sim\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1&-2&1\\\\0&2&1\\\\0&0&k-6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe last row requires $0=k-6$, so $k=6$."] [17592186120428 :question/problem "Given that $A =-3I$, where $I$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix, what is the value of $det(A)$?"] [17592186120526 :question/worked-solution "The order of the basis vectors matters. Here\n\n$$\nx=1b_1+0b_2-3b_3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_B=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\0\\\\-3\\end{bmatrix}$, so $x_1=1$."] [17592186134145 :question/worked-solution "Statement I is true because $A$ is $2\\times2$. Also,\n\n$$\nAA^T=\\begin{bmatrix}-1&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix}=I_2.\n$$\n\nThus statement II is true. A square matrix with $AA^T=I$ is orthogonal, so statement III is true. The correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""] [17592186134146 :question/worked-solution "Statement I is true because $A$ is $3\\times3$. However,\n\n$$\nAA^T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac54&0&0\\\\0&1&0\\\\0&0&\\frac54\\end{bmatrix}\\ne I_3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is false and $A$ is not orthogonal, so statement III is false. The correct answer is \"I only.\""] [17592186134241 :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix equals its transpose. Therefore,\n\n$$\nD^{-1}=D^T=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}&\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\\\-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}&-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186292858 :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB+AC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$4$</td><td>$3$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$0$</td><td>$-2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$5$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186292859 :question/problem "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AC+BC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$8\\sqrt{5}$</td><td>$-4$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$16$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$12$</td><td>$20$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186299802 :question/problem "Evaluate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AC+BC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>$0$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$0$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$3$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186299803 :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB+AC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$\\sqrt{3}$</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186299807 :question/problem "Calculate $CB-CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$CB-CA=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186299808 :question/problem "Calculate $AC-BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AC-BC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$4$</td><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$0$</td><td>$-4$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$4$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186365507 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $E=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${E}^{2}.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$E^{2}=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$-4$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$-2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$0$</td><td>{{field-5}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186365518 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${A}^{2}.$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$A^{2}=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$3$</td><td>$-3$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-4}}</td><td>$11$</td><td>{{field-5}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186485538 :question/problem "Calculate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AC+BC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-2}}</td><td>$4$</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$5$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186604606 :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB+AC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$5$</td><td>$7$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$3$</td><td>$-1$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$6$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$-3$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>"] [17592186604611 :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB+AC=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$-3$</td><td>$0$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$3$</td><td>$9$